  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1223 AM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nUpper level low will be weakening as it moves over the area on\nMonday and will be east of the area by Tuesday. Rain chances will\ncontinue south of Interstate 20 on Monday as weak lift persists \nwith this feature. Rainfall amounts are expected to be fairly\nlight though. High temperatures will be in the upper 60s and lower\n70s across the Big Country, where less cloud cover is expected,  \nwith highs in the mid 60s elsewhere. \n\nDry and seasonal weather returns to the area Tuesday through  \nthe end of the week, as northwest flow aloft develops between \na large upper trough over the eastern CONUS and ridging to our \nwest. Rain chances may return to the area by the end of next \nweekend, as a potential storm system approaches from the \nsouthwest.",
